1
00:00:12,480 --> 00:00:16,810
Mark introduces his method of learning Chinese

2
00:00:18,688 --> 00:00:20,547
You have only been in China for a year.

3
00:00:20,640 --> 00:00:22,530
He speaks Chinese so fluently.

4
00:00:22,740 --> 00:00:23,665
awesome!

5
00:00:25,380 --> 00:00:27,540
Actually my grammar is not very good.

6
00:00:27,810 --> 00:00:30,883
Many sentences are not quite accurate.

7
00:00:31,635 --> 00:00:35,186
But I see you have no problem communicating with Chinese people.

8
00:00:35,280 --> 00:00:36,540
how did you do it?

9
00:00:37,295 --> 00:00:39,845
I usually love my Chinese friends more.

10
00:00:40,199 --> 00:00:42,027
Chat with them often.

11
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:45,603
Listening and listening skills will naturally be greatly improved.

12
00:00:46,154 --> 00:00:49,574
Also, I suggest you stick to Chinese newspapers.

13
00:00:49,980 --> 00:00:52,657
You can learn a lot of new words this way.

14
00:00:53,370 --> 00:00:54,630
You are amazing!

15
00:00:54,774 --> 00:00:56,910
I can even read Chinese newspapers.

16
00:00:57,546 --> 00:00:59,856
It was definitely difficult at first.

17
00:01:00,120 --> 00:01:04,200
But when you encounter a word you don’t know, you can look it up in a dictionary.

18
00:01:04,530 --> 00:01:06,277
Then write it in a notebook.

19
00:01:06,990 --> 00:01:09,388
Take it out and review it when you have time.

20
00:01:09,690 --> 00:01:14,083
Slowly you will find that Chinese newspapers are not that difficult.

